-- and the other side, which the earlier theorem got wrong: two reports on one material whose values
-- disagree, together with one function agreeing with both -- the function being the count itself, and what
-- reconciles them being that their baths differ. A record that cannot tell this case from the Inventory's
-- is a record whose disagreements cannot be read in either direction: it will call a temperature series a
-- contradiction and a contradiction a difference of conditions.
br-cyh-consistent : (a : br-value Nat br-cyh-room ≡ br-value Nat br-cyh-cold → Empty) × ((b : count-bath (br-material Nat br-cyh-room) (br-bath Nat br-cyh-room) ≡ br-value Nat br-cyh-room) × (count-bath (br-material Nat br-cyh-cold) (br-bath Nat br-cyh-cold) ≡ br-value Nat br-cyh-cold))
br-cyh-consistent = (br-cyh-disagree , (m-cyh-room , m-cyh-cold))
